+# Receipts stopped
+
+For the volunteer on call when members say they get no receipts. Brings receipts back by starting the worker that
+sends them; while it is stopped, no member gets a receipt, and the ones queued are sent once it runs again. Written
+because receipts stopped three times and only Tomás knew the fix: once members waited until noon for him, and on
+October 29 the volunteer on call did not know what to do. Owner: the volunteer on call; Tomás is the one to call.
+
+The [worker](../architecture.md#parts) sends each receipt as a job from its queue in Postgres. On September 14 it
+had stopped right after a deploy, because the deploy restarts only the web app and leaves the worker stopped.
+
+## Before you begin
+
+- A shell on the server, with `sudo` to start the `larder-worker` service and `psql` access to the `larder` database.
+
+## Steps
+
+`scripts/restart-receipts-worker.sh` runs steps 1 to 4; run it on the server, or take the steps by hand.
+
+1. Check the worker: `systemctl status larder-worker`.
+
+   Expected: `inactive (dead)`, since a time shortly after the last deploy. If it says `active (running)`, the worker
+   is not the cause: go to [If it fails](#if-it-fails).
+2. Count the jobs waiting: `psql larder -c "select status, count(*) from procrastinate_jobs group by status"`.
+
+   Expected: a `todo` count, the receipts not yet sent; on September 14 it was 212 todo, 0 doing, 3 failed.
+3. Start the worker: `sudo systemctl start larder-worker`.
+
+   Expected: `systemctl status larder-worker` says `active (running)`.
+4. Run the query of step 2 again each minute until `todo` is 0.
+
+   Expected: `todo` falls, about 40 a minute on September 14, and reaches 0.
+5. Look at the `failed` count.
+
+   Expected: a few failed jobs. On September 14 the 3 failed were receipts that bounced because those members have no
+   valid email address; they need nothing from you.
+
+## If it fails
+
+- The worker stops again right after you start it: read its log, `journalctl -u larder-worker -n 50`, and call Tomás
+  with what it says.
+- The worker is running but receipts still do not arrive, or `todo` does not fall: call Tomás.
